{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> in the figure has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/87082784a051c7525966d9819cc379329a30e030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, all distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, \nare on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aaa2452d9ce4302e49ed83896ce666bd63e981c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/695e9c4e73387ea0d6bdc28d2d37fcfb7715e976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 2, DB = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />. If triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb27f6f4969ca28514e7183ed0e02ab68bbbe7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> \nhave equal areas, then that area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fdde55003bf41e0208ea11eb611aadc3c8bbea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10)); pair A=origin, B=(10,0), C=(8,7), F=7*dir(A--C), E=(10,0)+4*dir(B--C), D=4*dir(A--B); draw(A--B--C--A--E--F--D); pair point=incenter(A,B,C); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(point--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(point--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(point--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(point--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(point--E)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(point--F)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, (2,0), S); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (7,0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"478\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be715e9b0bce419cd9dccbb0fb6de7d63ebdf80e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{10}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"555\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301828b8af77c7c2cb4248d6cdb60ad8097c49e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DBEF] = [ABE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/caef471a11b502460364fad5d7066b087cf6bfa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DBEG] + [EFG] = [DBEG] + [ADG]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784731680f052ac94b3024014c87a8aebdc45e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[EFG] = [ADG]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. It therefore follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/58034f116bd0673b620f0106444757dbdc1b74d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADG] + [AGF] = [EFG] + [AGF]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a2953a78792495f0772305cfe55a6f520a0fe147.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADF] = [AFE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. Now, taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as the base of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e728a789f2ca839593526b82229b72fde61ec6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f2628c7bd8aba6794daadad02ce8f46d94c15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, and using the fact that triangles with the same base and same perpendicular height have the same area, we deduce that the perpendicular distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as the perpendicular distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. This in turn implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d43884618af677464b4058d06e9c6e73b4dbd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF \\parallel DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, and so as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f33127da7079f3e0385ffdfe0c2451b6a2c73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\parallel DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c69f0749dc92e388a8a5771c833b89fe9dae79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBE \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/47659b09c7034ce947a4116a7fdbd2350416a0a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BE}{BC} = \\frac{BD}{BA} = \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> have the same perpendicular height (taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as the base), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99a2b312f36461579efcf69cdee6f65a9ab2e3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABE] = \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot [ABC]=\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 10 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"257\" height=\"37\" />, and hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174129\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 268/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7646/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.380      1 -total\n 60.33%    8.676      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 37.60%    5.407      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15652:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174129 and revision id 282835. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}